Falsifies `kernel::arch::riscv64::iommu::proofs::the_root_entry_names_exactly_the_leaf`.

The defect is the leaf's physical address written into the non-leaf entry as it is, rather than
as a PPN at bit 10. The entry's PPN field starts at bit 10 while a page frame's address has zeros
below bit 12, so the IOMMU reads a PPN four times the leaf's and walks a frame the kernel never
allocated as this device's contexts.

Expected to fail: `assert!(((entry >> 10) & ((1 << 44) - 1)) << 12 == leaf, "the PPN is the leaf
entire")`. Confirmed red on 2026-11-11 (UTC), on an x86_64 host, against this file's pure functions
and harness compiled on their own.

The sibling harness `no_device_can_reach_another_devices_context` stays green under this patch:
it places devices and never builds a root entry.

--- a/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/arch/riscv64/iommu.rs
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@
 ///
 /// Name: provisional.
 fn non_leaf_entry(leaf: u64) -> u64 {
-    ((leaf >> 12) << 10) | NON_LEAF_ENTRY_VALID
+    leaf | NON_LEAF_ENTRY_VALID
 }
 
